==English==
{{was wotd|2010|June|26}}

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|reprobatus||disapproved, rejected, condemned}}, past participle of {{m|la|reprobo|reprobare}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛpɹəbət/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reprobate1.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|rare}} [[rejected|Rejected]]; cast off as worthless.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Jeremiah|6|30|text='''Reprobate''' silver shall men call them, because the Lord hath rejected them.}}
# Rejected by God; [[damned]], [[sinful]].
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=I|lines=696–7|passage=Strength and Art are easily out-done / By Spirits '''reprobate'''}}
# [[immoral|Immoral]], having no religious or principled character.
#: ''The '''reprobate''' criminal sneered at me.''
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=1|passage=And strength, and art, are easily outdone / By spirits '''reprobate'''.}}

